# Context compaction (workspace)

Mirrors **`~/z/env/ai/cursor/rules/chat-context-and-transcripts.mdc`** and **`meta-interactions.mdc`** so clones behave without the user’s global Cursor rules.

## Reading context

- Do **not** bulk-read **`~/.cursor/projects/.../agent-transcripts/`** or **`.chat/`**.
- Prefer **`docs/AGENT_TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY.md`**, then **`docs/AGENT_TRANSCRIPT_DIGEST.md`** if present, then **`docs/AI_CONTEXT.md`**, **`AGENTS.md`**, **`docs/PROJECT_PROMPT.md`**.

## Writing

- Compact session notes: **`.chat/YYYY-MM-DD-topic.md`**.
- Substantive outcomes: append to **`docs/AGENT_TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY.md`**.

## Indexing

- Repo root **`.cursorignore`** must list **`.chat/`** and **`.vscode/`**. The agent **write tool may be unable to edit `.cursorignore`** — use the editor or:  
  `printf '%s\n' '.chat/' '.vscode/' >> .cursorignore`  
  then `git add -f .cursorignore` if needed.

## Remote activity

- For SSH/VM/cloud work, write activity on the remote machine at `docs/remote/REMOTE_ACTIVITY_LOG.md` first.
- Sync the remote log back into local `docs/remote/` (e.g. `REMOTE_ACTIVITY_LOG.<host>.md`).
